      "problem": "${\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{6}{|3x+9|\\sqrt{x^2+6x+10}} \\textrm{d}x= }$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we complete the square for the argument of the square root in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+6x+10 & ={x}^{2}+2\\cdot 3x+{3}^{2}-{3}^{2}+10 \\\\  & =(x+3)^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{6}{|3x\\!+\\!9|\\sqrt{x^2\\!+\\!6x\\!+\\!10}} \\,\\textrm{d}x  = \\int  \\dfrac{6}{3|x\\!+\\!3|\\sqrt {1\\!+\\!(x\\!+\\!3)^2} }\t\\, \\textrm{d}x = {2} \\int \\dfrac{1}{|x\\!+\\!3|\\sqrt{1\\!+\\!(x\\!+\\!3)^2}} \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet $u = x+3.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=1\n\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n\\textrm{d}x = \\textrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}2\\int \\frac{1}{|x+3|\\sqrt{1+(x+3)^{2}}}\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{1+{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡u+C \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(x+3)+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
